    "lawCode": "Amd §13-357, NYC Ad Cd; amd §§506, 507, 510, 511 & 512, R & SS L",
    "lawSection": "New York City Administrative Code",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S7736\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the administrative code of the city of\nNew York and the retirement and social security law, in relation to\nthe disability benefits of members of the New York city fire\ndepartment pension fund\n\nPURPOSE:\n\nThe legislative proposal will provide Tier 3 fire pension fund members\nwho were hired after July 1, 2009; the same ordinary and accidental\ndisability pension's afforded to Tier 1 and Tier 2 members.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThe legislative proposal will provide Tier 3 fire pension fund members\nwho were hired after July 1, 2009; the same ordinary and accidental\ndisability pension's afforded to Tier 1 and Tier 2 members. This\nproposal explicitly includes FDNY employees who service the NYC Fire\nDepartment as medical officers and hold a uniform rank.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill will provide much needed parity amongst the ranks of all\nFDNY employees including medical officers employed by the NYC Fire\nDepartment. This bill provides Tier 3 fire pension fund members who\nwere hired after July 1, 2009; the same ordinary and accidental\ndisability pension's afforded to Tier 1 and Tier 2 members. After the\nexpiration of Tier 2 uniformed firefighters, officers and medical\nofficers lost the benefit of ordinary and accidental disability\npensions. This bill will correct this loss and provide parity across\nall uniformed firefighters, officer and medical officers in the City\nof New York.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nSee the fiscal.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nThis act shall take effect on the sixtieth day after becoming law.\n\n",
